  "term": "involuntary response",
  "definition": "An involuntary response is a complex automatic reaction to a sudden strong stimulus. It typically includes moving away from the stimulus, muscle tightening with bending of the limbs, blinking, and changes in heart rate, blood pressure, and breathing.",
